An explicit --assignee wins over LINEAR_ISSUE_CREATE_ASSIGN_SELF=always.
-- seed.json --
{"User": [{"id": "1b000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002", "name": "Jane Developer", "displayName": "jane"}]}
-- env --
LINEAR_ISSUE_CREATE_ASSIGN_SELF=always
-- run --
linear issue create --title "Assigned to Jane" --team ENG --assignee jane --no-interactive
-- stdout --
✓ Created issue ENG-1: Assigned to Jane
https://linear.app/kadoraba/issue/ENG-1/assigned-to-jane
-- stderr --
ENG-1 has no --project or --parent. Decide ownership from the candidate Project's full content and the related Initiative content (linear guide issue-authoring), then save the original read and set the project: (if [ -e original.json ] || [ -L original.json ]; then echo 'original.json exists' >&2; exit 1; fi; t=$(mktemp original.json.XXXXXX) || exit; s=0; linear issue view 'ENG-1' --json >| "$t" || { cat "$t" >&2; s=1; }; [ "$s" != 0 ] || ln "$t" original.json || s=1; rm -f "$t"; exit "$s") && linear issue update 'ENG-1' --project <project> --base-file original.json
-- state.json --
{"Issue": [{"title": "Assigned to Jane", "assignee": "1b000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002"}]}
